                <pb facs="0873" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg753"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Decision of the admiralty court, November 20, 1904, re
                        steamer Arabia.</hi></head>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>To consider the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Arabia</hi> as having been
                        arrested on sufficient ground.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The cargo, consisting of 500 sacks of flour, belonging to Messrs. Runge
                        &amp; Thomas, as well as 5,000 sacks belonging to Messrs. Dodwell &amp; Co.,
                        to be considered as noncontraband. The decision of the Vladivostok prize
                        court in this respect to be reversed and the said cargo to be set
                        free.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The decision of the Vladivostok prize court as relates to the remainder of
                        the cargo to remain in force, no appeal from it having been taken.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
